    "keywords": "accounting, trial balance, profit and loss, balance sheet, journal, reports, ledger",
    "body": "# Accounting reports\n\n## What this is\nThe formal books behind the shop: journals, trial balance, profit & loss and balance sheet, fed automatically by orders, payments, purchasing and the cashbook.\n\n## Where to find it\n**Operations & finance**, then the **Accounting** tab. Needs the **accounting** module.\n\n## Read the reports\n- **Trial balance** — every account's debit/credit totals; it must balance. If it doesn't, stop and find the journal causing it.\n- **Profit & loss** — income minus expenses for a chosen period. Pick dates in your business timezone; totals follow those local days.\n- **Balance sheet** — what the business owns and owes on a chosen date.\n- **Journals** — the double-entry story behind every transaction; open one to see exactly which accounts moved.\n\n## Exports\nUse **Export CSV** on the Customers/Orders/Payments screens and **Ledger CSV** on the Payments page for accountant-friendly files.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Judging profit from the till. Cash in the drawer ignores dues, stock and unpaid supplier bills — profit & loss does not.\n- Picking report dates in a different timezone mindset. The app uses your business timezone for day boundaries.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **accounting:read**. Account setup changes need **accounting:manage** and should be rare and deliberate.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nAccounting reports asal munafa aur kul position dikhatay hain — sirf drawer ki cash nahi. Trial balance hamesha barabar hona chahiye; na ho to journal check karein."
