    "audience": "business",
    "keywords": "cashbook, cash, bank, account, transaction, expense, transfer, reconciliation",
    "body": "# Cashbook — daily cash and bank\n\n## What this is\nThe day book for real money: cash in the drawer, bank balance, expenses and transfers between accounts.\n\n## Where to find it\n**Operations & finance**, then the **Cashbook** tab. Needs the **cashbook** module.\n\n## Record money movement\n1. Pick the account (Cash, Bank…).\n2. Choose the kind: **Receipt** (money in), **Expense** (money out) or **Transfer** (between your own accounts).\n3. Type amount, date, reference and a memo your future self will understand (\"Electricity bill March\", not \"bill\").\n4. Save. Each entry also posts the matching accounting journal automatically.\n\n## Reconciliation\nWhen the bank statement arrives, compare statement lines with cashbook entries for the period; differences are missing entries or bank charges — record them, never force the total.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Using the cashbook for customer payments. Those belong on the order (**Record payment**) so the customer's balance stays right; the cashbook then receives its entry automatically through accounting setup.\n- Back-dating without a memo. Dates can be corrected, but write why.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **cashbook:read**; entries need **cashbook:write**. Many owners keep entry rights with one trusted person.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nCashbook rozana ki asal raqam ka khata hai — drawer ki cash, bank, kharchay. Customer ki payment order par likhein, cashbook mein nahi; warna customer ka balance ghalat ho jayega."
