    "title": "Catalog and price list",
    "audience": "business",
    "keywords": "catalog, price list, item, sku, price, inactive",
    "body": "# Catalog and price list\n\n## What this is\nYour ready price list: the items you sell again and again, with prices, so orders start from a tap instead of typing.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb: **Catalog**. Mobile: **More**, then **Catalog**. Needs the **catalog** module switched on.\n\n## Add an item\n1. Choose **Add item**, pick its item type, name and unit (piece, metre…).\n2. Set the selling price. Link a stock variant if the item consumes inventory.\n3. Save — it becomes selectable on new orders.\n\n## Stop selling an item\nMark it **inactive** instead of deleting. Old orders keep their prices; the item just leaves the pickers.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Changing a price and expecting old orders to change. They never do — an order keeps the price agreed that day.\n- Two catalog items with the same name. Add the difference to the name (for example \"Suit — premium stitching\").\n\n## Permission warnings\nManaged by **orders:write** holders; the module itself is switched on by **settings:manage**.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nCatalog aap ki price list hai. Jo item bikna band ho jaye use inactive kar dein — purane orders ki qeematein nahi badalti. Naye orders mein catalog se item chunna typing se tez aur ghalti se pak hai."
