    "keywords": "customer, add customer, phone, whatsapp consent, archive, restore, export",
    "body": "# Customers\n\n## What this is\nYour customer book: names, mobile numbers, notes, order history and saved measurements.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb: **Customers**. Mobile: **More**, then **Customers** (or search from the home screen).\n\n## Add a customer\n1. Choose **Add a customer**.\n2. Type the full name and mobile number. Add notes only if the whole team should see them.\n3. Save. If the number already exists, the app warns you instead of making a duplicate.\n\n## What happens next\nThe customer appears in search, can be picked on new orders, and their orders and measurements collect under their name.\n\n## WhatsApp consent\nTick consent only when the customer agrees to WhatsApp messages. If a customer opts out later, use **WhatsApp consent** on their card — messages stop, history stays.\n\n## Archive and restore\nFinished with a customer (duplicate, left the area)? Open their card and choose **Archive**. Nothing is deleted — history stays safe. To bring them back: **Show archived** → **Restore**. You are asked to confirm before archiving.\n\n## Export\n**Export CSV** downloads your customer list (name, phone, consent, notes) for Excel or backups.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Two spellings of one name create two customers. Search first, then add.\n- Writing private remarks in notes — every staff member with customer access can read them.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **customers:read**; adding, editing and archiving need **customers:write**.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nCustomer add karne ke liye naam aur mobile number likhein. Khatam shuda customer ko delete nahi, **Archive** karein — tareekh mehfooz rehti hai, aur **Show archived** se wapas bhi aa jata hai. WhatsApp consent sirf tab tick karein jab customer raazi ho."
