    "id": "faq",
    "title": "FAQ and troubleshooting",
    "audience": "all",
    "keywords": "faq, help, problem, cannot, forgot password, locked out, offline, error, slow, missing button",
    "body": "# FAQ and troubleshooting\n\n## I forgot my password. Where is the reset link?\nThere isn't one — by design. Ask your business owner (or, for owners, the platform team) to use **Reset password** in Team settings. You will get a temporary password, sign in, and immediately choose your own. See *Staff, roles and passwords*.\n\n## A button or whole section is missing for me.\nTwo usual causes: your **role** lacks the permission, or the owner switched the **module** off. Both are fixed by the owner in settings — not by reinstalling anything.\n\n## The app says I am offline / read-only.\nCheck the device connection. The web workspace turns read-only offline so nobody creates conflicting records; mobile keeps showing your downloaded data. Try again when the connection returns — nothing you saved online is lost.\n\n## I saved an order and the connection dropped. Is it duplicated?\nNo. Order saving uses a one-time save key: retrying the same save returns the original order instead of a twin. Check the Orders list before creating another.\n\n## A payment was typed wrong.\nNever look for an edit button — there is none, on purpose. **Reverse** the payment with a reason, then record the correct one. Both show in history. See *Payments, receipts and exports*.\n\n## The customer says they never got the WhatsApp.\nOpen **WhatsApp notifications** history: queued/sent/failed is shown with the reason. Also confirm the customer consented and the number (with country code) is right.\n\n## Why did writes stop with a subscription message?\nYour plan period and grace days ended, or a plan cap (customers/staff/monthly orders) was reached. The owner renews under **Subscription & billing**; after platform approval, writes resume.\n\n## Numbers look wrong on the dashboard today.\nDashboards use your business timezone for \"today\". If the shop's timezone setting is wrong, days shift — owners fix it in Business settings. Money totals always come from posted payments, never from typing.\n\n## We archived the wrong customer/order/business.\nNothing is lost. **Show archived** → **Restore** (businesses: the platform team's Archived filter). History and payments return exactly as they were.\n\n## Who changed this record?\nAsk an owner to check the business **audit history** (platform team: platform Audit history). Every privileged change records who, when and what.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nPassword bhool jayein to owner se reset karwayein — email link nahi aata. Button ghayab ho to aksar permission ya module band hota hai. Ghalat payment edit nahi hoti; reverse karke sahi darj karein. Jo cheez archive ho jaye woh hamesha wapas aa sakti hai."
