    "keywords": "inventory, stock, material, variant, movement, wastage, reorder, valuation",
    "body": "# Inventory and stock\n\n## What this is\nFabric, buttons, zips and everything you consume: how much came in, what was used, what is left, and what it is worth.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb and mobile: **Operations & finance**, then the **Inventory** tab. Needs the **inventory** module.\n\n## Record stock\n1. Create the item and its variants (colour/size).\n2. Use movements: **Receipt** when stock arrives, **CONSUMPTION** (shown as Consumption) when an order uses it, **Wastage** for damage, **Adjustment** for count corrections (always with the real counted number).\n3. A movement that was wrong is **reversed** with a reason — never edited or deleted. Reversing asks for the reason.\n\n## Reorder alerts\nSet a reorder point per variant; the alert list shows what to buy before it runs out.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Typing consumption guesses. Count what the order actually used; small daily truth beats a monthly surprise.\n- Negative stock is blocked on purpose. Record the receipt first, then the consumption.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **inventory:read**; movements need **inventory:write**.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nStock ki har harkat likhein: aamad (Receipt), istemal (Consumption), zaya (Wastage). Ghalat entry delete nahi hoti — wajah likh kar **reverse** karein. Stock minus mein nahi ja sakta; pehle aamad darj karein."
