    "body": "# Measurements\n\n## What this is\nEach customer's saved sizes. Every save creates a dated **revision** — old measurements are never overwritten, so a fitting mistake can always be traced.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb: **Measurements**. Mobile: **More**, then **Measurements**.\n\n## Save measurements\n1. Choose the customer and a measurement template (for example Shalwar Kameez).\n2. Type each measurement in the unit shown. Text fields accept words (for example \"loose fit\").\n3. Add notes for anything unusual, then **Save revision**.\n\n## What happens next\nThe new revision becomes the latest one. Orders can attach the measurement profile so the tailor works from exactly these numbers.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Editing in your head and saving twice \"to be sure\". Two revisions are created — harmless, but pick the right one on the order.\n- Measuring over thick clothing without noting it. Write it in notes.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **measurements:read**; saving needs **measurements:write**. Measuring is often a tailor's job while order-taking is the counter's — roles can separate them.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nHar customer ke naap revision ki surat mein save hote hain — purane naap kabhi khatam nahi hote. Naya naap save karne se woh latest ban jata hai, aur order par wahi profile lagta hai."
