    "keywords": "onboarding, setup, owner, template, stages, workflow, modules, branding",
    "body": "# Setting up your business (owner checklist)\n\n## What this is\nThe one-time setup that makes the app speak your shop's language: your item names, your workflow stages, your receipt branding.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb: **Business settings**. Mobile: **More**, then the Business settings item.\n\n## Steps\n1. **Name and logo** — set the name customers should see on receipts and invoices. Pick a logo style and colours, or paste a logo URL.\n2. **Modules** — switch on only what you use (Catalog, Inventory, Purchasing, Cashbook, Accounting…). Hidden modules disappear from everyone's menu.\n3. **Item types** — add the things you sell (for example Shalwar Kameez, Suit, Alteration). Orders and the catalog use these names everywhere.\n4. **Workflow stages** — check the stages an order passes through (for example Cutting → Stitching → Fitting → Ready). The first stage is where new orders start.\n5. **Payment methods** — choose which methods you accept (Cash, Bank, Digital).\n6. **Custom fields** — add extra boxes you always need (for example fabric type on an order, or neck size on a customer).\n7. Invite your team from **Team** (see *Staff and roles*) and give each person the smallest role that lets them do their job.\n\n## What you type\nNames exactly as customers should read them — they appear on receipts and WhatsApp messages.\n\n## What happens next\nSettings apply immediately for everyone. Workflow or field changes only affect new screens; old orders keep the history they were created with.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Turning on every module at once. Start with Customers, Orders and Payments; add ERP modules when you need them.\n- Renaming stages after orders exist. Old orders keep their stage history; new orders use the new stages.\n\n## Permission warnings\nOnly accounts with **settings:manage** can change setup. Owners should keep at least one trusted second admin.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nPehli dafa: business ka naam aur logo set karein, sirf woh modules on karein jo istemal honge, apni items aur order stages check karein, phir team ko invite karein. Settings sab par foran lagu ho jati hain."
