    "title": "Suppliers and purchasing",
    "audience": "business",
    "keywords": "supplier, purchase order, receiving, settlement, ledger, pay supplier",
    "body": "# Suppliers and purchasing\n\n## What this is\nWho you buy from, what you ordered, what actually arrived, and what you still owe them.\n\n## Where to find it\n**Operations & finance**, then the **Suppliers / Purchasing** tabs. Needs the **suppliers** and **purchasing** modules.\n\n## Buy something\n1. Add the supplier once (name, phone).\n2. Create a purchase order with lines: item, quantity, agreed cost.\n3. When goods arrive, **Receive** against the order — type what really arrived, not what was promised.\n4. **Settle** when you pay: amount, account, reference. Part payments are fine; the supplier ledger keeps the running balance.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Receiving the full order when half arrived. Short receiving keeps stock and dues honest.\n- Paying without a settlement entry. Cash leaves, the ledger still shows a debt.\n\n## Permission warnings\nViewing needs **suppliers:read** / **purchasing:read**; buying and settling need the matching **:write** permissions.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nSupplier se khareed ka pura record: order, asal aamad, aur adaigi. Jitna maal aaya utna hi receive karein, aur har adaigi settlement mein likhein — supplier ka khata khud baqi rakam dikha dega."
