    "keywords": "whatsapp, notification, message, template, consent, opt out, delivery, history",
    "body": "# WhatsApp notifications\n\n## What this is\nAutomatic customer messages — order confirmed, payment received, order ready — plus the delivery history that proves what was sent.\n\n## Where to find it\nWeb: **WhatsApp notifications**. Mobile: **More**, then **Notifications**.\n\n## How it works\n1. The platform team connects one sender number and approves message templates with Meta.\n2. When an order is created, a payment recorded or an order becomes ready, the app queues the matching message for customers who consented.\n3. The history shows each message: queued, sent, delivered, or failed with the reason.\n\n## Consent matters\nMessages only go to customers who agreed (see *Customers*). If someone replies STOP or asks you directly, remove consent on their customer card — no new messages queue for them.\n\n## Common mistakes\n- Assuming a queued message was delivered. Check history; a failed message shows why (wrong number, template issue).\n- Editing template wording casually. Templates are approved text — changes need platform approval again.\n\n## Permission warnings\nHistory needs **notifications:read**. Template settings are owner-level (**settings:manage**) plus platform approval.\n\n## Roman Urdu mein\nOrder, payment aur ready honay par customer ko khud-ba-khud WhatsApp jata hai — sirf un ko jinhon ne consent diya ho. Message gaya ya nahi, tareekh (history) mein wajah ke sath nazar aata hai."
